\summary{Thesis class for Kyiv Polytechnic Institute per DSTU 3008:2015}
\begin{description}
A LaTeX class for the bachelor diploma project and courseworks of Igor Sikorsky Kyiv
Polytechnic Institute, Faculty of Informatics and Computer Engineering, typeset per the
Ukrainian standard DSTU 3008:2015 and the department guide. It covers the whole diploma
package: title page, assignment, Ukrainian and English abstracts with counted pages,
figures, tables, sources and appendices, the project sheet and A3 drawing sheets with ESKD
title blocks, tables continued across pages, and a biblatex style for reference lists per
DSTU 8302:2015.

The class needs LuaLaTeX. It uses Times New Roman and Courier New, required by the guide,
and falls back to TeX Gyre Termes and Cursor where they are missing. The documentation is
in Ukrainian.
\end{description}
\begin{announcement}
Version 2.1.0 adds kpi-thesis-dstu, a biblatex style (biber backend) for Ukrainian reference
lists per DSTU 8302:2015: books with 1-3 authors in the heading and 4+ after the title,
journal articles, collections and proceedings, theses, standards, laws, patents, web pages
and repositories, with DOI or URL and access date, and English and Russian sources in their
own language. The class turns it on with \kpisetup{bibliography=biblatex,
bib-resource=sources.bib}; the order of sources is set with sources=citation, alphabetical
or chronological. Documents with a hand-written thebibliography build as before.
\end{announcement}
\begin{note}\end{note}
